TASK-260715-zwtrhy,task,run-physical-m4-product-security-and-accessibility-matrix,"Run the physical M4 product, security, privacy, and accessibility matrix",backlog,STORY-260715-n5dt84,,"Execute the final M4 user-journey matrix on one named physical iPhone and one named Apple-silicon Mac after all feature and test tasks are review-ready. Validate the real Network Extension permission/session, system indicator, user-controlled SSH host, full/degraded/reasserting/failure explanations, diagnostics, privacy, migration, and accessibility.","In scope: device/OS/Xcode/source/dependency revisions, approved test host/keys, fresh and returning users, profile/key import or generation, first trust, repeat trust, changed key, auth/passphrase errors, privacy acknowledgement, VPN permission/system approval, connect, full/degraded/reasserting/failure, QUIC/route settings display, app suspend/terminate/relaunch, disconnect, diagnostics/export/delete, legacy branch on Mac, locale/pseudo rows feasible on device, VoiceOver, keyboard, text scaling, screenshots/video, counters, redaction, cleanup, and pass/fail. Out of scope: production credentials/traffic, release signing/TestFlight/App Store, M1-M3 throughput/leak matrices except referenced evidence, regional licensing, and unsupported devices.","1. On both devices a user can configure, trust, acknowledge privacy, grant permission, connect, understand authoritative full/degraded/reasserting/failure state, inspect/export/delete diagnostics, and disconnect with system VPN status matching the provider. 2. Changed host key stops before auth; credentials remain in the approved Keychain boundary; app termination does not stop an active provider; diagnostics/export contain no prohibited markers. 3. Mac legacy behavior matches the approved coexist/migrate/retire decision with idempotency/rollback evidence and the preserved legacy build/release contract referenced. 4. VoiceOver completes the iPhone journey and VoiceOver plus keyboard complete the Mac journey at supported text scaling/contrast/motion settings with no critical accessibility blocker. 5. A TASK-ID-scoped redacted evidence bundle records matrix rows, environments, opaque fixture IDs, screenshots, system/capability state, export manifest/hash/categories, accessibility observations, cleanup, linked M1-M3 evidence, and explicit pass/fail.","[""TASK-260715-1fk4ja"",""TASK-260715-1kfqgp"",""TASK-260715-3b6krz"",""TASK-260715-132kb2"",""TASK-260715-3nzx7s"",""TASK-260715-3f4rhy"",""TASK-260715-2qr5aj"",""TASK-260715-2wqffe"",""TASK-260715-3nkhry"",""TASK-260715-10phgg"",""TASK-260715-3hvz8n""]",[],"[{""text"":""Deliver the stated scope while preserving every explicit non-scope boundary"",""done"":false},{""text"":""Verify every acceptance criterion with the specified automated or manual evidence"",""done"":false},{""text"":""Attach a TASK-260715-zwtrhy-scoped redacted outcome with commands artifacts and residual risks"",""done"":false}]",,2026-07-15T02:38:19Z,2026-07-15T02:47:33Z,true,[],[],[]

