nt \\\"Serialized promotion\\\" as Promote\\n}\\n\\nnode \\\"macOS GitHub Environment\\\" as MacEnv\\nnode \\\"iOS App Store Environment\\\" as IOSEnv\\nnode \\\"Relay staging / provenance\\\" as RelayEnv\\nartifact \\\"Redacted evidence bundle\\\" as Evidence\\n\\nFork --> PRCI : read-only token\\\\nno production secrets\\nMaintainer --> PRCI : same required gates\\nPRCI --> Evidence : results + digests\\nTrigger --> Manifest : approved immutable commit\\nEvidence --> Manifest : all blocking checks pass\\nManifest --> Promote\\nPromote --> MacEnv : scoped Developer ID/notary/GitHub credentials\\nPromote --> IOSEnv : scoped Apple Distribution/App Store credentials\\nPromote --> RelayEnv : verified staged bytes only\\nMacEnv --> Evidence\\nIOSEnv --> Evidence\\nRelayEnv --> Evidence\\n\\nnote bottom of PRCI\\nNo protected environment, signing material,\\npublication token, or privileged runner is\\nreachable from pull-request code.\\nend note\\n@enduml\", type=outcome, description=\"PlantUML CI trust-boundary planning diagram\"); add_resource(TASK-260715-1tzaed, name=\"TASK-260715-1tzaed_macos-release-sequence.puml\", content=\"@startuml\\n"'!theme plain'"\\ntitle TASK-260715-1tzaed — macOS signed distribution sequence\\n\\nparticipant \\\"Release orchestrator\\\" as Orchestrator\\nparticipant \\\"Archive builder\\\" as Builder\\nparticipant \\\"Bundle/entitlement inspector\\\" as Inspector\\nparticipant \\\"Protected signer\\\" as Signer\\nparticipant \\\"DMG packager\\\" as Packager\\nparticipant \\\"Apple notary service\\\" as Notary\\nparticipant \\\"Private GitHub release\\\" as GitHub\\nparticipant \\\"Clean supported Mac\\\" as Mac\\n\\nOrchestrator -> Builder : immutable source + versions + accepted relay staging digest\\nBuilder --> Orchestrator : unsigned archive + inventory + hashes\\nOrchestrator -> Inspector : verify host/extension topology and pre-sign inputs\\nInspector --> Orchestrator : exact matrix pass\\nOrchestrator -> Signer : sign nested code inside-out\\\\nminimum entitlements + hardened runtime\\nSigner -> Inspector : signed application\\nInspector --> Orchestrator : strict signatures + actual entitlements pass\\nOrchestrator -> Packager : signed application digest\\nPackager --> Orchestrator : versioned and stable-name DMG bytes + checksums\\nOrchestrator -> Notary : submit exact candidate digest\\nNotary --> Orchestrator : accepted request + log\\nOrchestrator -> Packager : staple and verify ticket\\nPackager -> Mac : quarantined Gatekeeper/install smoke\\nMac --> Orchestrator : install/upgrade/extension/rollback evidence\\nOrchestrator -> GitHub : publish immutable versioned asset\\\\nthen verified stable authenticated asset\\nGitHub --> Orchestrator : remote sizes, hashes, release IDs\\n@enduml\", type=outcome, description=\"PlantUML macOS release sequence planning diagram\"); add_resource(TASK-260715-3661ps, name=\"TASK-260715-3661ps_ios-testflight-sequence.puml\", content=\"@startuml\\n"'!theme plain'"\\ntitle TASK-260715-3661ps — iOS archive and TestFlight sequence\\n\\nparticipant \\\"Release orchestrator\\\" as Orchestrator\\nparticipant \\\"Version allocator\\\" as Version\\nparticipant \\\"Protected archive builder\\\" as Builder\\nparticipant \\\"Bundle/profile inspector\\\" as Inspector\\nparticipant \\\"App Store Connect\\\" as ASC\\nparticipant \\\"Physical iPhone\\\" as Device\\nparticipant \\\"Release operations\\\" as Ops\\n\\nOrchestrator -> Version : approved tag + immutable candidate\\nVersion -> ASC : query existing builds\\nASC --> Version : monotonic build state\\nVersion --> Orchestrator : marketing version + reserved build number\\nOrchestrator -> Builder : exact source, locks, relay staging, versions\\nBuilder --> Orchestrator : signed xcarchive/export + hashes\\nOrchestrator -> Inspector : profiles, entitlements, topology, privacy manifests, symbols\\nInspector --> Orchestrator : technical preflight pass\\nOrchestrator -> ASC : upload exact candidate\\nASC --> Orchestrator : processed build ID\\nOrchestrator -> ASC : assign approved TestFlight group\\nASC -> Device : install unchanged processed build\\nDevice --> Orchestrator : entitlement/lifecycle/accessibility evidence\\nOrchestrator -> Inspector : server + local binary preflight\\nInspector --> Ops : accepted build ID + provenance + technical compliance evidence\\n\\nnote over Builder,ASC\\nNo rebuild, resign, profile substitution,\\nor resource change may inherit TestFlight evidence.\\nend note\\n@enduml\", type=outcome, description=\"PlantUML iOS archive and TestFlight sequence planning diagram\"); add_resource(TASK-260715-29r0k8, name=\"TASK-260715-29r0k8_release-gate-dependency.dot\", content=\"digraph ReleaseGate {\\n  graph [rankdir=TB, label=\\\"TASK-260715-29r0k8 — Release gate dependency\\\", labelloc=t, fontsize=18];\\n  node [shape=box, style=\\\"rounded,filled\\\", fontname=\\\"Helvetica\\\"];\\n  edge [fontname=\\\"Helvetica\\\"];\\n\\n  ci [label=\\\"CI threat model accepted\\\", fillcolor=\\\"#D9EAF7\\\"];\\n  relay [label=\\\"Relay staging + compliance audit accepted\\\", fillcolor=\\\"#D9EAF7\\\"];\\n  mac [label=\\\"macOS distribution verdict accepted\\\", fillcolor=\\\"#D9EAF7\\\"];\\n  ios [label=\\\"iOS distribution verdict accepted\\\", fillcolor=\\\"#D9EAF7\\\"];\\n  legal [label=\\\"Current Apple + privacy + legal + regional approvals\\\", fillcolor=\\\"#FFF2CC\\\"];\\n  review [label=\\\"Review fixture, instructions, metadata, package audit\\\", fillcolor=\\\"#FFF2CC\\\"];\\n  rc [label=\\\"Exact-candidate regression matrix\\\", fillcolor=\\\"#D9EAD3\\\"];\\n  claims [label=\\\"Behavior-to-claim audit\\\", fillcolor=\\\"#D9EAD3\\\"];\\n  go [shape=diamond, label=\\\"Go / hold / reject\\\", fillcolor=\\\"#FCE5CD\\\"];\\n  submit [label=\\\"Submit exact App Store Connect build\\\", fillcolor=\\\"#D9EAD3\\\"];\\n  response [label=\\\"Review response / revalidation / resubmission\\\", fillcolor=\\\"#D9EAD3\\\"];\\n  channels [label=\\\"Channel verification + rollback watch\\\", fillcolor=\\\"#D9EAD3\\\"];\\n\\n  ci -> relay;\\n  relay -> mac;\\n  relay -> ios;\\n  mac -> rc;\\n  ios -> rc;\\n  legal -> claims;\\n  review -> claims;\\n  rc -> claims;\\n  claims -> go;\\n  go -> submit [label=\\\"go\\\"];\\n  go -> rc [label=\\\"hold/rework\\\"];\\n  submit -> response;\\n  response -> channels;\\n}\", type=outcome, description=\"Graphviz detailed release gate dependency diagram source\"); add_resource(EPIC-260715-w5gzf4, name=\"EPIC-260715-w5gzf4_diagram-render-validation.md\", content=\"# Diagram render validation\\n\\nDate: 2026-07-15\\n\\nThe canonical plan query and board validation passed. The planning snapshot was saved through task-board.\\n\\nBoth task-board render attempts failed before producing an image:\\n\\n- task-board plan EPIC-260715-w5gzf4 --render --layout phases --format png\\n- task-board plan EPIC-260715-w5gzf4 --render --layout hierarchy --format png\\n\\nGraphviz dot aborted because the installed Homebrew binary could not load /opt/homebrew/opt/libtool/lib/libltdl.7.dylib.\\n\\nNo workstation package mutation was authorized or performed. The attached DOT and PlantUML sources are the authoritative diagrams-as-code. Repairing the local Graphviz/libtool installation and rerunning task-board render is a tooling follow-up, not a product dependency.\", type=outcome, description=\"Diagram renderer validation and Graphviz environment anomaly\"); add_resource(EPIC-260715-w5gzf4, name=\"EPIC-260715-w5gzf4_logbook.md\", content=\"# M5 solution-architecture logbook\\n\\n## 2026-07-15 — Distribution starts from accepted platform and product evidence\\n\\nM5 does not prove Apple packet-tunnel intended use, provisioning viability, generated target architecture, relay protocol behavior, routing safety, or M4 product behavior again. Exact task links consume Gate A0, Gate P0, generated-target, M1 routing, M2 portable-relay, and M4 physical product/security evidence before credentials or publication.\\n\\n## 2026-07-15 — Stable private GitHub assets require authentication\\n\\nReluxProxy.dmg may keep a stable name, but a private repository cannot be treated as an anonymous download origin. The publication and acceptance tasks require authenticated retrieval, checksum verification, immutable versioned assets, and a stable update sequence that never mixes versions.\\n\\n## 2026-07-15 — Reproducibility boundary differs by artifact\\n\\nUnsigned relay assets must reproduce bit-for-bit from pinned inputs. Apple-signed archives, profiles, and timestamps introduce expected signed-output variation, so macOS and iOS tasks preserve reproducible source, locks, generated project, relay bytes, unsigned inputs, and exact signed-output provenance rather than making an invalid byte-identical IPA claim.\\n\\n## 2026-07-15 — Legal and review decisions are explicit gates\\n\\nRegional VPN licensing/storefront availability, current Apple rule revalidation, public privacy policy, App Privacy/export declarations, and review-host credentials require accountable external owners. These are first-class blocking tasks; engineering assumptions cannot close them.\\n\\n## 2026-07-15 — Dependency ownership was kept acyclic\\n\\nRelay produces audited staging bytes; Apple distribution consumes them and verifies archived copies. iOS produces technical privacy, API, symbol, and encryption inventories; release operations owns final legal declarations and App Review materials. This boundary avoids circular release dependencies.\\n\\n## 2026-07-15 — Renderer anomaly\\n\\nBoard validation and canonical planning passed, but local Graphviz rendering failed because dot cannot load libltdl.7.dylib. Diagram sources and the exact anomaly are attached; no package installation or source/specification edit was performed.\", type=outcome, description=\"Architecture findings, decisions, boundaries, and renderer anomaly\"); set_notes(EPIC-260715-w5gzf4, text=\"Solution-architecture logbook 2026-07-15: created a 67-task planning-only decomposition with 249 exact dependencies. Key boundaries: CI before M5 relay supply chain; audited relay staging before parallel macOS/iOS distribution; exact candidate evidence before privacy/legal/App Review operations. Stable private GitHub assets require authenticated retrieval. Relay bytes are bit-for-bit reproducible; Apple signed outputs use reproducible unsigned inputs plus exact signed provenance. Regional VPN licensing, current Apple guidance, public privacy/export declarations, release credentials, and review fixture are explicit blocking tasks. Board validation and canonical plan pass. Graphviz PNG rendering is currently unavailable because dot cannot load libltdl.7.dylib; authoritative DOT/PlantUML sources are attached. No implementation or source/specification edit was performed.\")'" in /Users/iv/Developer/relux-proxy
