ble commit and validated version manifest can enter protected release environments; pull-request and arbitrary-branch code cannot invoke production credentials. 2. macOS, iOS, relay, GitHub publication, and App Store Connect permissions are separately scoped and supplied only to the job that needs them. 3. A single production release is active at a time and retries are idempotent, reuse the same candidate inputs, and cannot duplicate versions or publish a mixed release. 4. Cancellation or any stage failure records state, revokes temporary material, withholds dependent publication, and emits an actionable resumable or rollback disposition. 5. Dry-run and controlled-failure tests prove approvals, job ordering, environment isolation, serialization, secret masking, and no partial promotion.","assignee":"","blockedBy":["TASK-260715-2wjvlx","TASK-260715-2hef52","TASK-260715-2759wy"],"blocks":["TASK-260715-vg2of8","TASK-260715-3gkwn0","TASK-260715-3sk5cd","TASK-260715-1njthi","TASK-260715-8g5fpa","TASK-260715-1vo4rm","TASK-260715-sfkrzq","TASK-260715-29r0k8","TASK-260715-6j1u2g"],"checklist":[{"text":"Deliver the stated scope while preserving every explicit non-scope boundary","done":false},{"text":"Verify every acceptance criterion with the specified automated or manual evidence","done":false},{"text":"Attach a TASK-260715-2ybl7y-scoped redacted outcome with commands, artifacts, and residual risks","done":false}],"children":[],"created":"2026-07-15T03:00:25Z","description":"Build the release-only workflow layer that consumes already-verified inputs, enters protected environments, serializes production publication, and delegates macOS, iOS, relay, and evidence jobs without exposing credentials to untrusted code.","id":"TASK-260715-2ybl7y","isBlocked":true,"name":"implement-protected-serialized-release-orchestration","notes":"","outcomeResources":[],"parent":"STORY-260715-anxje6","preconditionResources":[],"scope":"In scope: trusted tag or approved dispatch entry, immutable